SYNTHETIC – a gzip-compressed log (two fictitious lines compressed with mtime 0), as if a rotated
log had been delivered instead of a text log; it starts with the gzip magic bytes 1F 8B and
contains NUL bytes; keep the bytes, see .gitattributes.
Expected from LogExcerpt.build: kind binary, detected GZIP, no charset and no lines, hint
"Binary content is not returned".
Used by LogExcerptTest (tasks.md T015, research D-10).
